event('212-4-degree-three','targeted proof check','The opening quadruple repeats the preceding off-by-one nerve description. A degree-three simplex has four vertices and three arrows; its component is the triple composable fibre product of R, as follows by two applications of the corrected recurrence. The corrected layer changes quadruple to triple; the printed layer keeps quadruple. The degree-three component is the one in which associativity and the compatibility of the elementary nerve operations are tested.','212, p. 110, first three lines')
event('212-4-equivalence-groupoid','targeted proof check','An equivalence relation has exactly one arrow from a to b when a is related to b, and none otherwise. Reflexivity supplies identities, transitivity supplies the unique composite, and symmetry supplies inverses. Uniqueness gives all category identities. Applied naturally to every T-point, this gives the internal groupoid by Yoneda; no additional choice of composition remains for a genuine equivalence relation.','212, p. 110, second paragraph')
event('212-4-action-category','targeted proof check','The arrow (g,a) goes from a to ga. Thus (g prime,ga) after (g,a) has label g prime g and source a, exactly the displayed formula. Associativity and identities follow from the monoid action laws. If G is a group, the inverse is (g inverse,ga). Hom(a,b) consists of all g with ga=b, so the transporter description follows.','212, p. 110, action-category paragraph and display')
event('212-4-action-groupoid-iff','refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','Refined statement id: 212-4-action-category-nonempty. The converse as printed needs a nonemptiness or detection hypothesis: in Sets take X empty and any monoid that is not a group, for example the additive nonnegative integers. The empty action category is a groupoid, although G is not a group. If X is nonempty, choose a in X; an inverse to (g,a) has some label h and its two composite identities force hg=gh=1, proving the converse. In an arbitrary category an analogous conclusion requires a hypothesis allowing the product with X to detect the required isomorphism; pointwise nonemptiness cannot be silently assumed. The printed biconditional is retained in both layers and the qualification is reserved for the notes.','212, p. 110, sentence si et seulement si G est un groupe')
event('212-4-universe-remark','carried as background without fault found','The remark fixes a universe so the collections of small categories and simplicial sets can be treated in a larger ambient set-theoretic setting. No new set-theoretic axiom or existence proof for universes is supplied by the text or claimed by this audit.','212, p. 110, REMARQUE')
event('212-5.1-i','independent re-proof','For b in B, form the characteristic polynomial of multiplication by p2 prime(b) on the finite projective B-algebra C via p1 prime. Its rank may vary: choose a common upper bound N and multiply each locally constant rank-r characteristic polynomial by T^(N-r). An arrow from x to y identifies the outgoing-arrow schemes at y and x by composition, preserving their targets. Hence the two pullbacks of this monic polynomial to the relation agree, coefficient by coefficient, including the rank padding; every coefficient lies in A. Cayley-Hamilton makes p2 prime(b) a root in C. Restricting along the identity section makes b a root in B. Thus every b is integral over A. The finite-projective characteristic polynomial and Cayley-Hamilton are standard algebraic inputs; the invariant-coefficient argument has been checked here using the groupoid composition.','212, p. 110, Theorem 5.1(i)')
record_page('212',110,r'''Compared sources/fr_printed/fr/212.tex entry lines 510–560 and sources/fr/fr/212.tex entry lines 513–563 with scan leaf 13 at 400 dpi, full page and all three enlarged bands. Inspected the degree-three count, order of action composition, semicolon, heading typography, script groupoid R versus ordinary component R_1, and every prime on the ring homomorphisms.

Both layers restore spaced punctuation and abbreviations, the unpunctuated composition display, semicolon, ordinary quotes, roman remark and underlined section heading, the script groupoid letter, inline equalizer pair, primes instead of stars, wavy category letters and upright mathematics. The corrected layer changes quadruple to triple, linked to the corrected degree convention on p. 109; the printed layer preserves quadruple.

Checked the relation and action groupoid constructions. The unqualified converse from action groupoid to group is false for an empty acted-on set, and the precise nonempty-set refinement is recorded without rewriting the historical claim. Established Theorem 5.1(i) by the invariant characteristic-polynomial argument; the rest of the theorem continues on p. 111.''')
